# Laziness proof: $take does not force the tail thunk when n reaches zero.
# The third element of the seq is an error sentinel. After taking 2 elements,
# take(0, tail) returns Seq.End immediately without forcing `tail`,
# so the raise never fires (B-383 fix, S-896: now uses tinct Seq.Cons syntax).
[collect [take 2 [Seq.Cons head: 1  tail: [Seq.Cons head: 2  tail: [Seq.Cons head: [raise "tail past n should not fire"]  tail: Seq.End]]]]]
=== out
Dict({0: Int(1), 1: Int(2)})
